to-be-incorporated-into-paper-150 = unlines (cons "In hyperactivity's language as the repository implements it: A shared subterm is held by a duplicating cell that copies lazily, one level at a time as it is" (cons "read. A stored value lives once, and readers copy its top cell. A substitution of dimensions is" (cons "recorded on the reference, not applied by copying. A subterm in a position that might not be read" (cons "is held unbuilt until an operation meets it: `fst (a , b)` never computes `b`, even if `b`" (cons "diverges. `delay e` holds `e` so wherever it stands: it has `e`'s type, an operation meeting it" (cons "builds it, `force` of it is it, and its code is `cthunk` (the first-order and C++ back ends," (cons "being strict, compute it where it stands). A λ's subterms that do not mention its variable are computed once, however often the λ is" (cons "applied. A case is one cell, and selecting a branch is one step." nil))))))))
